cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it and the M-ABSA benchmark. Paper publication details will be added after acceptance."
title: "Cross-Lingual Aspect-Based Sentiment Analysis of E-Commerce Reviews with Memory-Efficient QLoRA-Adapted Qwen3-4B"
abstract: >-
  Compares three adaptation strategies for cross-lingual aspect-based sentiment
  analysis on a single 8 GB consumer GPU: zero-shot prompting, three-shot
  prompting with English examples, and QLoRA adapter training on English data.
  Evaluated on the M-ABSA benchmark over three domains and six languages with
  two task formulations, scored by exact-tuple micro-F1.
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/mzain4/crosslingual-absa-qwen3"
keywords:
  - aspect-based sentiment analysis
  - cross-lingual transfer
  - few-shot prompting
  - QLoRA
  - parameter-efficient fine-tuning
  - large language models
  - M-ABSA
